/-!
# Literal degree-64 Hall--Janko matrix data

Generated by `source/generate_data.py` from the preserved ATLAS
J2G1-f4r64aB0 generators and rank-one/trace discovery records. Bit j of a row's
first plane gives the coefficient of 1, and bit j of its second plane the
coefficient of t. Thus codes 0,1,2,3 mean 0,1,t,t+1=t².

Left orbit words are reversed for column action; right and algebra words keep
the displayed order. Polynomial coefficients are constant-first. Signed trace
letters are retained verbatim. These definitions assert no matrix identities.
See `../source/README.md` and `../../Source.md` for source attribution.
-/

